@startuml AI_Enhanced_Architecture

title AI-Enhanced EM Log Analyser Architecture

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "LoGAnalyser System (AI-Enhanced)" {
    
    package "Main Controller" {
        [EM_Analyzer_main] as Main
    }
    
    package "Configuration Layer" {
        [configSettings] as Config
        database "Configs" {
            file "Pattern Configs (JSON)"
            file "AI Model Config"
        }
    }
    
    package "Analysis Layer (Hybrid)" {
        
        rectangle "Pattern-Based Analysis" #E3F2FD {
            [Traditional Analyzer] as PatternAnalyzer
            [PatternMatching] as Pattern
            [TracePatternMatching] as TracePattern
        }
        
        rectangle "AI-Powered Analysis" #FFF9C4 {
            [AI_Analyzer] as AIAnalyzer
            [ML Model] as Model
            [Preprocessor] as Preprocess
            [Postprocessor] as Postprocess
        }
        
        [Result Fusion] as Fusion
    }
    
    package "ML Infrastructure" #FFE0B2 {
        [Model Server] as ModelServer
        [Feedback Collector] as Feedback
        [Model Monitor] as Monitor
        [Retraining Pipeline] as Retrain
    }
    
    package "Data Layer" {
        database "Training Data" {
            folder "Labeled Logs"
            folder "Historical Tickets"
            folder "Analyst Feedback"
        }
        
        database "Model Storage" {
            file "log_analyzer_v1.pt"
            file "log_analyzer_v2.pt"
            file "tokenizer/"
        }
    }
    
}

cloud "External Systems" {
    [JIRA Server] as JIRA
    node "GPU Cluster" as GPU
}

database "File System" {
    folder "Logs & Results"
    file "Dashboards"
}

' Main workflow connections
Main --> Config: load configs
Main --> PatternAnalyzer: pattern analysis
Main --> AIAnalyzer: AI analysis
PatternAnalyzer --> Fusion: results
AIAnalyzer --> Fusion: predictions
Fusion --> Main: combined results

' Pattern analyzer connections
PatternAnalyzer --> Pattern: uses
PatternAnalyzer --> TracePattern: uses

' AI analyzer connections
AIAnalyzer --> Preprocess: preprocess logs
Preprocess --> Model: tokenized input
Model --> Postprocess: raw predictions
Postprocess --> AIAnalyzer: formatted results

' Model server connections (optional)
AIAnalyzer ..> ModelServer: REST API (optional)
ModelServer --> Model: loads model
ModelServer --> GPU: inference

' Model storage connections
Model --> "Model Storage": load/save
Preprocess --> "Model Storage": load tokenizer

' Feedback loop
Main --> Feedback: collect analyst feedback
Feedback --> "Training Data": store feedback
JIRA --> Feedback: resolution data

' Monitoring
AIAnalyzer --> Monitor: log predictions
Monitor --> "Training Data": store metrics

' Retraining pipeline
Monitor --> Retrain: trigger retraining
"Training Data" --> Retrain: load data
Retrain --> Model: retrain
Retrain --> "Model Storage": save new version

' External connections
Main --> JIRA: fetch/update
Main --> "File System": read/write

note right of Fusion
Combines both approaches:
- Pattern-based: Known issues
- AI-based: Unknown issues
- Confidence-weighted fusion
end note

note right of Model
Hybrid Architecture:
- BERT for text encoding
- MLP for metadata
- Multi-task learning:
  * Root cause
  * Severity
  * Components
end note

note bottom of Retrain
Continuous Learning:
- Automated retraining
- Performance monitoring
- A/B testing
- Version management
end note

@enduml
